  "facts": [
    "Toven Tunnel, Norway's longest at 10,665 metres, opened on 22 November 2014 after four years of construction that began in 2010, reshaping travel across Nordland's rugged coastline.",
    "By replacing a narrow, steep, twisting road along Vefsnfjorden, the tunnel cuts County Road 78 by eight kilometres, slashing travel time by 10–20 minutes for commuters and freight alike.",
    "The 1,460‑million‑kroner project, including new road links, was partially financed through a 405‑million‑kroner toll, ensuring sustainable maintenance for this vital artery."
